# UI design

Tokens live in `src/styles/theme.css`. Change a color, radius, or font there. Do not restyle a primitive by overriding its classes at the call site. If a primitive needs a new look, add a variant to it in `src/components/ui`.

The reference product fails because every category has its own hue, headings and rows share one size, section gaps vary, and corner radii do not match. Fix those four things. Do not add decoration to compensate.

Stories live in `src/components/stories`. Use realistic privacy-ops content (requests, subjects, regulations, consent), not placeholder text.

## Color

Palette is zinc neutrals plus one indigo `primary`.

`primary` is for the one main action, the active nav item, the focus ring, and the first chart series.

Surfaces: `canvas` behind the page, `card` for panels, `background` for controls and dialogs, `muted` for tracks and hovers.

Status tones exist only inside `Badge` (`neutral`, `info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`) and `Alert` (`warning`, `destructive`). Do not color the row, the button, and the chart for the same fact.

Category, department, regulation, and request type are labels. Use `Badge variant='outline'` or `secondary`. They do not get their own hue.

Charts use `chart-1`, then `chart-2`, `chart-3` (an indigo ramp), then the neutral `chart-4`, `chart-5`.

## Type

Inter is `font-sans`. Geist Mono is `font-mono`, used for record IDs (`DSR-20418`) and nothing else.

| Role | Classes |
|---|---|
| Page title | `text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight` |
| Section / card title | `text-sm font-semibold tracking-tight` |
| Key figure | `text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight tabular-nums` |
| Body, row, control | `text-sm` |
| Meta, axis, hint, table header | `text-xs text-muted-foreground` |
| Record ID | `font-mono text-xs` |

A heading and the text under it must not share a size. Numbers that are compared use `tabular-nums`.

## Density

Controls are `h-8` (sm `h-7`, lg `h-9`). Badges are `h-5`. Table rows are `h-11`, headers `h-9`.

## Spacing

One step between sibling sections: `gap-4`.

Card inset is the `--card-spacing` variable (20px). Do not add `p-*` to a `Card`; use `CardHeader`, `CardContent`, `CardFooter`.

Inside a card, stack with `gap-3` or `gap-4`, not both in the same card.

Page canvas padding is `p-6`.

## Radius

Radii nest: the outer element is always rounder than what sits inside it.

| Element | Class |
|---|---|
| Card, dialog, sheet, table frame, floating sidebar | `rounded-2xl` |
| Menu, popover, select list, alert | `rounded-xl` |
| Button, input, select trigger, tabs list | `rounded-lg` |
| Menu item, tab trigger, nav item | `rounded-md` |
| Checkbox | `rounded-sm` |
| Badge, avatar, switch, progress | `rounded-full` |

Do not set an arbitrary radius (`rounded-[10px]`), and do not mix scales on siblings.

## Elevation

Panels use `ring-1 ring-foreground/[0.07] shadow-xs`, not a hard `border`. Floating layers (menu, popover) use `border shadow-lg`. Modal layers (dialog, sheet) use `shadow-xl`.
